# What image/test-image.sh expects of an image booted in QEMU (generic ALARM kernel, no phone
# hardware, no Android container). One rule per line, a reason after "#":
#   active UNIT    the unit must be active after the boot
#   fails UNIT     the unit may fail: it needs the phone
#   restarts UNIT  the unit may keep restarting: it needs the phone; one that must be active
#                  too may then also be found activating, between two starts
# Every other failed or restarting unit is an error of the image.

active dbus.service
active systemd-logind.service
active polkit.service
active NetworkManager.service
active plinius-pacman-init.service   # pacman keyring of the phone, made at the first start
active greetd.service                # first start: the PIN prompt of plinius-greeter
active sshd.service

fails mount-android-system.service                  # Android's system image (loop device on the phone's data)
fails android-set-boot-completion-property.service  # the Android container (bionic libc, libcutils)
fails plinius-bootcheck.service                     # androidboot.slot_suffix from the phone's bootloader
fails plinius-gpu.service                           # the Mali GPU's /sys/kernel/ged
# The generic kernel 7.x refuses a helper of its cgroup device program (-EINVAL); the phone's 6.1
# loads it. A newer phone kernel would need the program changed.
fails plinius-appaccessd.service

restarts plinius-charge.service          # charger in /sys/devices/platform/charger
restarts plinius-usb.service             # USB and pogo pins in /sys/usb
restarts plinius-wake.service            # touch and motion sensors of the phone
restarts plinius-backlight-wake.service  # the display's card0-DSI-1 and lcd-backlight
restarts plinius-sar.service             # the modem's radio HAL through /dev/binder
restarts vibrator-ff-bridge.service      # Android's vibrator HAL through binder
restarts plinius-appaccessd.service      # see above
# First start without a PIN: the greeter's phoc finds no GPU in QEMU ("Found 0 GPUs"), the
# greeter ends and greetd starts it again. It still has to be active (or between two starts).
restarts greetd.service
